      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From a typical statistical standpoint, Zone 2 exhibits several indicators often associated with higher perceived risk in predictive models, such as lower median income and a higher density of nightlife venues. While Zone 1 has certain demographic traits, the lower presence of late-night venues might suggest a different underlying crime profile. A policing algorithm would likely flag Zone 2 for more frequent patrol presence due to the combined factors of socioeconomic stress and concentrated retail activity.",
